# Live desk config (user 2026-09-16 — wins over everything earlier)

This file is the policy source of truth. It overrides v1 divergent DB defaults, older `.cursorrules` / chat memory, and any doc that still says `TIMEFRAME=15m` only, `RSI_LONG_MAX=30`, `MAX_DAILY_LOSS_USD=50`, or `LEVEL_CROSS_UP` in `ALLOWED_TYPES`.

Copy numbers from local `.env` / `.env.example`. Do not “realign to v1” unless the user asks.

## Exec / safety (unchanged)

- `EXEC_MODE=hub_demo`, `BITGET_DEMO=1`, `BITGET_ALLOW_LIVE=0`
- Never bypass `risk/gate.py`. Size with `risk/sizing.py`
- Do not commit `.env` or `data/*.jsonl` / `data/*.json`
- Do not mutate `C:\divergent`
- `PAPER_FALLBACK=0` — Demo catalog only. Paper-live PnL is not Demo equity

## Scan / signals

- `TIMEFRAMES=15m,1h,4h` (also set on `TIMEFRAME` as a comma list). Loop + public WS scan **all three**. Do not collapse back to 15m-only
- Hard trade ban: `USDCUSDT` (`USDC/USDT:USDT`). Stablecoin basis pair — drop from scan and deny at the risk gate. Extra bans via `TRADE_DENY_SYMBOLS`. Do not re-enable unless the user asks
- `ALLOWED_TYPES=BULLISH_DIV,BEARISH_DIV,LEVEL_CROSS_DOWN` — **no** `LEVEL_CROSS_UP`
- `LEVEL_CROSS_DOWN` → long; `LEVEL_CROSS_UP` → short (detector still exists, just not allowed)
- `ALLOW_LONG=1`, `ALLOW_SHORT=1`
- `RSI_LONG_MAX=0` — zone **off**. Do not restore 30. Code default is 0. Longs with RSI 20–69 are valid; still skip `rsi_extreme_long` (≥70) / `rsi_extreme_short` (≤30)
- `TF_BLOCKER_ENABLED=0` — leave off even though 15m is no longer the only TF. Pair blocker stays on

## Risk

- `RISK_USD_PER_TRADE=10`, `MAX_NOTIONAL_USD=500`, `MIN_NOTIONAL_USD=10`
- `MAX_POSITIONS=15`
- `MAX_SAME_DIRECTION_POSITIONS=4` (correlation guard; alias `CORRELATION_GUARD_MAX`)
- `MAX_DAILY_LOSS_USD=150` (not 50)
- `COOLDOWN_SEC=900`
- Dollar stop: `MAX_LOSS_PCT_OF_MARGIN=40`, `DOLLAR_STOP_SL_PCT_THRESHOLD=0`
- rToken / stocks: `RTOKEN_ATR_TF=1h`, `RTOKEN_ATR_FLOOR_PCT=0`, `RTOKEN_ATR_PCT_MIN=0.5` (no crypto 2% ATR floor). Crypto stays `ATR_PCT_MIN=0.3` + 2% floor on the signal TF

## BTC filters

- `BTC_REGIME_TF=4h`, `BTC_REGIME_ENABLED=1`, `BTC_EMA50_FILTER_ENABLED=0`
- Momentum `1.2%` / `4h`. Symmetric: bearish blocks long, bullish blocks short
- Do not restore `BTC_REGIME_TF=1h` unless the user asks

## Hub

- `HUB_LEVERAGE=20` is the **cap**. Opens use adaptive lev: `max(2, min(20, int(35 / SL%)))` so SL ≈ 35% of margin
- `PAPER_LEVERAGE=1` — `size_usd` is notional
- v3 `/trade/fills` must be filtered by symbol (+ qty); dummy BTC@65000 never hits live `data/paper_fills.jsonl`

## Price sanity (Demo vs public)

- Thin Demo books drift from the public feed. **BZ** (2026-09-18): Demo `103.52` vs public `~99` (4.5%). **LTC** (2026-09-19): Demo `59.78` vs public `~58` (3.0%) — paper SL `@57.99` booked `−14.97` while hub `exec_pnl ≈ −0.26`. Live Demo mark still ~3% above public.
- Open guard: `SIGNAL_PRICE_MAX_DEV_PCT=2.5` (all), `RTOKEN_SIGNAL_PRICE_MAX_DEV_PCT=2.5`. Also reject fill vs **signal** price. Old crypto `5%` let LTC through. (`DemoPriceMismatchError` → flatten.)
- Exit guard: `MARK_SANITY_MAX_DEV_PCT=2.5` / `RTOKEN_MARK_SANITY_MAX_DEV_PCT=2.5`. Drop a public mark that disagrees with **position entry** (Demo fill) or candle. Hub TPSL on the exchange stays the real exit.
- Exchange `/equity` + `/fills` (`exec_pnl`) stay the monetary source of truth; paper-shadow PnL is a diagnostic and can diverge on these gaps.
